      "explanation": "Rapid onset (within ~15 minutes) of respiratory symptoms (shallow breathing, chest tightness), perioral tingling, and new blotchy rash after a wasp sting strongly suggests anaphylaxis/ systemic allergic reaction. Clinician appropriately concerned and advised ambulance/antihistamine.",
      "supporting_evidence": [
        "Temporal relationship: symptoms began ~15 minutes after wasp sting.",
        "Respiratory involvement: patient reports shallow breathing and chest tightness.",
        "Mucocutaneous signs: lip tingling and blotchy rash (urticaria/erythema) consistent with systemic allergic reaction.",
        "No prior tolerance: patient reports this has not happened before (no prior sting anaphylaxis history, so new severe reaction possible)."
      ],
      "opposing_evidence": [
