      "explanation": "Allergic exposures can trigger bronchospasm in patients with reactive airways disease. If the patient had undiagnosed asthma or reactive airways, the sting could precipitate wheeze/tightness. However, no prior asthma history or reported wheeze makes this less likely than anaphylaxis.",
      "supporting_evidence": [
        "Acute chest tightness and sensation of shallow breathing may reflect bronchospasm.",
